IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Ofek Hadash — the shared ontology`

-- ===========================================================================
-- OFEK HADASH ("New Horizon"), the Israeli teachers' pay reform.
--
-- This module declares the nouns. Every other module in this encoding reads
-- its types from here and adds rules; nothing here decides anything.
--
-- SOURCE. The collective agreement of 25 December 2008 between the State of
-- Israel and the Teachers' Union (Histadrut HaMorim), implementing the Ofek
-- Hadash reform, together with the wage agreement of 19 October 2022 and the
-- approved collective agreement of 29 June 2026. Article numbers cited as
-- "§ n" below are articles of the 2008 base agreement unless another
-- instrument is named.
--
-- The corpus these are read from is
--   https://morimovilimcatala.github.io/ofek-hadash-corpus/
-- whose own caveats are reproduced in NOTES.md. Hebrew terms are given in
-- transliteration with the Hebrew beside them, because the instruments name
-- these things in Hebrew and a reader checking this against the agreement
-- needs the word that appears on the page.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Who the reform applies to`

-- § 3: the agreement applies to employees graded in the TEACHING GRADE
-- (dirug ovdei hora'a) employed in kindergartens, primary schools and junior
-- high schools, including special education. § 7 then defines the persons.

-- § 7(d)-(h): the qualification ladder. A teacher is academic (holds a
-- recognised degree), certified, senior-certified, or unqualified. The
-- distinction drives WHICH salary table applies (§ 36) and, for existing
-- teachers, which conversion chapter (§§ 43-50 academic, §§ 51-61 not).
DECLARE `a teaching qualification` IS ONE OF
    `academic — holds a recognised first degree`      -- § 7(d), (e)
    `academic — holds a recognised second degree`
    `academic — holds a doctorate`
    `certified but not academic`                      -- § 7(f) mo're musmach
    `senior certified but not academic`               -- § 7(g) mo're bachir
    `unqualified`                                     -- § 7(h)

-- § 36(c)-(d): the table a teacher is placed in is selected by degree, and
-- the RATING CODE (kod dirug) printed on the table's own heading identifies
-- it. 101 is the BA table, 102 the MA table; a doctorate is placed in the
-- MA table and paid a further 5% (§ 36(d)(2)).
DECLARE `a salary table` IS ONE OF
    `the BA table — rating code 101`
    `the MA table — rating code 102`

-- § 7(i)-(j): an EXISTING teacher (mo're kayam) was employed before the
-- reform reached their school and crosses over by CONVERSION (hamara,
-- §§ 43-50); a NEW teacher (mo're chadash) starts inside the reform and is
-- placed at rank 1, seniority 0 (§ 36(a)).
DECLARE `how the teacher entered the reform` IS ONE OF
    `a new teacher placed under section 36`
    `an existing teacher converted under sections 43 to 50`

-- §§ 15-22: the working week differs by the stage of education, because the
-- frontal / individual / presence split does. Only the two stages the 2008
-- agreement sets out in full are carried here; see NOTES.md on what is not.
DECLARE `a stage of education` IS ONE OF
    `a primary school`            -- § 15  beit sefer yesodi
    `a junior high school`        -- § 17  chativat beinayim

-- § 39(a): the role supplements (gmulei tafkid) that SURVIVE into the
-- reform, in the order the article lists them. § 39(a)(3) and (4) are the
-- special-education supplements, which § 39(b) excludes from the "combined
-- salary for a full post" basis, so they are named separately below.
DECLARE `a role carrying a supplement` IS ONE OF
    `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade`   -- § 39(a)(1)
    `homeroom teacher of a first-grade class`                  -- § 39(a)(2)
    `subject coordinator`                                      -- § 39(a)(5)
    `road-safety coordinator`                                  -- § 39(a)(6)
    `security coordinator`                                     -- § 39(a)(7)
    `social-education coordinator`                             -- § 39(a)(8)
    `grade-level coordinator`                                  -- § 39(a)(9)
    `laboratory coordinator`                                   -- § 39(a)(10)
    `assessment and measurement coordinator`                   -- § 39(a)(11)

§§ `The teacher, as one record`

-- The whole encoding takes one record and reads fields off it. This is the
-- house style: one GIVEN parameter, one shape to document, one JSON object
-- at the API boundary.
--
-- SENIORITY (vetek, § 37) is recognised teaching seniority as the Teachers'
-- Service Regulations (takanon) define it, excluding the internship year but
-- including teaching service in the IDF or national teaching service. It is
-- an INPUT here: the takanon's own recognition rules are not encoded, and
-- NOTES.md records that as the largest single gap.
--
-- RANK (darga, §§ 36, 38) is the 1-to-9 rank. It is likewise an input: § 38
-- makes promotion depend on ministry criteria and, for ranks 7 to 9, on
-- evaluations and a system-wide quota, none of which is a function of this
-- record.
DECLARE `a teacher` HAS
    `qualification`                IS A `a teaching qualification`
    `seniority in years`           IS A NUMBER   -- § 37, vetek
    `rank`                         IS A NUMBER   -- §§ 36, 38, darga, 1..9
    `stage of education`           IS A `a stage of education`
    `how they entered`             IS A `how the teacher entered the reform`
    `fraction of a full post`      IS A NUMBER   -- § 33, 1 means 100%
    `roles`                        IS A LIST OF `a role carrying a supplement`
    `classes in the coordinated grade level` IS A NUMBER  -- § 39(a)(9), 0 if none
    `units of the school-role supplement`    IS A NUMBER  -- 2022 § 22, 0 if none
    `teaches special education`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- § 39(a)(3)
    `special education percentage` IS A NUMBER   -- § 39(a)(3): 5.5, 8.5, 9 or 14

§§ `Reading the record`

GIVEN `the teacher` IS A `a teacher`
GIVETH A `a salary table`
`the table the teacher is placed in` `the teacher`
    @nlg the salary table %the teacher% is placed in
    MEANS
    -- § 36(c): first degree to the first-degree table; second degree to the
    -- second-degree table; § 36(d)(1) places a doctorate in the SECOND-degree
    -- table, and pays the 5% separately.
    CONSIDER `the teacher`'s `qualification`
    WHEN `academic — holds a recognised first degree`  THEN `the BA table — rating code 101`
    WHEN `academic — holds a recognised second degree` THEN `the MA table — rating code 102`
    WHEN `academic — holds a doctorate`                THEN `the MA table — rating code 102`
    -- §§ 51-53 give teachers who are not academic their own tables. Those
    -- tables are NOT in the corpus this encoding reads (NOTES.md § 4), so a
    -- non-academic teacher is placed in the BA table here and the encoding
    -- says so rather than inventing a table.
    OTHERWISE                                          `the BA table — rating code 101`

GIVEN `the teacher` IS A `a teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the teacher is academic` IF
    -- § 7(d): "academic teacher" for the purposes the reform uses it for.
    CONSIDER `the teacher`'s `qualification`
    WHEN `academic — holds a recognised first degree`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `academic — holds a recognised second degree` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `academic — holds a doctorate`                THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                          FALSE

GIVEN `the teacher` IS A `a teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the teacher holds a doctorate` IF
    -- § 36(d)(2): the 5% doctorate supplement hangs off this alone.
    CONSIDER `the teacher`'s `qualification`
    WHEN `academic — holds a doctorate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                           FALSE

§§ `Illustrations`

-- A teacher used by every module downstream as the running example: a
-- BA-qualified junior-high homeroom teacher, eleven years in, rank 4, full
-- post. The numbers she produces are traced through NOTES.md § 6.
`Yael` MEANS `a teacher` WITH
    `qualification`                IS `academic — holds a recognised first degree`
    `seniority in years`           IS 11
    `rank`                         IS 4
    `stage of education`           IS `a junior high school`
    `how they entered`             IS `a new teacher placed under section 36`
    `fraction of a full post`      IS 1
    `roles`                        IS LIST `homeroom teacher of a class other than the first grade`
    `classes in the coordinated grade level` IS 0
    `units of the school-role supplement`    IS 0
    `teaches special education`    IS FALSE
    `special education percentage` IS 0

-- A second-degree primary-school teacher at the top of the table, holding
-- two supplements and three units of the 2022 school-role supplement.
`Dvora` MEANS `a teacher` WITH
    `qualification`                IS `academic — holds a recognised second degree`
    `seniority in years`           IS 30
    `rank`                         IS 8
    `stage of education`           IS `a primary school`
    `how they entered`             IS `an existing teacher converted under sections 43 to 50`
    `fraction of a full post`      IS 1
    `roles`                        IS LIST `homeroom teacher of a first-grade class`
                                        , `subject coordinator`
    `classes in the coordinated grade level` IS 0
    `units of the school-role supplement`    IS 3
    `teaches special education`    IS FALSE
    `special education percentage` IS 0

-- A half-post doctorate holder, to exercise § 36(d)(2) and the § 33
-- pro-rating together.
`Noa` MEANS `a teacher` WITH
    `qualification`                IS `academic — holds a doctorate`
    `seniority in years`           IS 6
    `rank`                         IS 3
    `stage of education`           IS `a junior high school`
    `how they entered`             IS `a new teacher placed under section 36`
    `fraction of a full post`      IS 50%
    `roles`                        IS EMPTY
    `classes in the coordinated grade level` IS 0
    `units of the school-role supplement`    IS 0
    `teaches special education`    IS FALSE
    `special education percentage` IS 0

#ASSERT `the table the teacher is placed in` `Yael`  EQUALS `the BA table — rating code 101`
#ASSERT `the table the teacher is placed in` `Dvora` EQUALS `the MA table — rating code 102`
#ASSERT `the table the teacher is placed in` `Noa`   EQUALS `the MA table — rating code 102`
#ASSERT `the teacher is academic` `Yael`
#ASSERT `the teacher holds a doctorate` `Noa`
#ASSERT NOT `the teacher holds a doctorate` `Yael`
